{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/602088-obfuscated-car-chase","id":602088,"title":"Obfuscated Car Chase","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-24T12:34:58-07:00","id":602088,"title":"Obfuscated Car Chase","content":"Well, not a car <i>chase</i>, but the following idea that a player came up with:<br /> <br /> A capable user of Obfuscate uses Touch of Shadows on a car and races it at high speed through a city with decent night traffic. The player's idea is that people will not consciously perceive the car (so no police will chase after them etc.), but people will still subconsciously veer to the side and perform other evasive maneuvers (just like people don't bump into the desk given as an example in the rules).<br /> <br /> How would you handle that?<br /> <br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li> Does this actually work, or does driving at high speed &quot;obviously draw attention&quot; to the car?</li> <li> If it works and people do not conciously perceive the car, will they be able to perform evasive maneuvers? Does the fact that they only perceive it subconsciously affect their reaction time?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> I tend to think that this shouldn't work.<br /> I can go along with using Cloak of Night on the car, so no one will notice it. But no one will take evasive measures, either.<br /> I can also see that one might use The Familiar Stranger on the car to make it appear like an ambulance or police car with wailing sirens.<br /> <br /> But with Touch of Shadows? I tend to rule it out.<br /> <br /> I'd be glad to hear your thoughts on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T13:03:48-07:00","id":602153,"title":"","content":"I also think it wouldn't work because, as you say, it draws obvious attention. It's not &quot;normal&quot; behavior for a car to be zipping around dangerously like that. I still think it's an awesome way to handle a car chase, and now I will endeavor to throw such a scenario at my players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T13:33:22-07:00","id":602228,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think driving at high speeds would attract attention and break the Obfuscate. But as long as you're obeying traffic laws and setting your speed by the cars around you, no one will notice that your car is panted neon orange with lime green stripes, you left tail light is out, your trunk is wide open, and you have no license plates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T14:03:06-07:00","id":602248,"title":"","content":"I think the above posters are right.<br /> <br /> But I also believe you could make a devotion that would allow for something more specifically like what you, and the rest of us no doubt, want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T16:55:38-07:00","id":602367,"title":"","content":"You get penalties if the object is larger than the vampire using Size. The suggested modifiers only include 3 Sizes larger so that is going to limit you, sports car is 10. Assuming a regular sized person, 10 is going to be the largest object you could allow, and you would be stretching things out of the norm. It fails outright, seemingly, if the vampire forces people to interact with the object. A parked car would be fine, but driving in traffic seems like that requires interaction. Driving at high speeds in traffic definitely is forcing interaction. I think the suggested usage is going to far. I think you would need 3 dots of Obfuscate to make it happen. A devotion at that level would be even better. At 4 dots, you could go with an emergency vehicle to less covertly do what you want without much issue. At 5 dots, you could probably do it with a semi truck with a trailer. A mobile Oubliette, that is certainly novel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 07-24-2015, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T20:18:03-07:00","id":602480,"title":"","content":"No reason to think that insane idea should work. That said, no reason to think the char would know without try.<br /> <br /> Tell your player you decided, and that the character have to discover things himself, or make someone else discover.<br /> <br /> During tests you can convey the answer and the why through actual scenes of the limits being stretched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T04:32:19-07:00","id":602788,"title":"","content":"If you can't Obfuscate the car <i>during</i> the high speed chase, then before there's too many cops and a helicopter overhead, you could drive through an alley and when unseen come out, obey the rules of the road, drive safely, and use it to make sure that no one is noticing the bullet holes and the previously identifiable go faster stripes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T07:59:08-07:00","id":602960,"title":"","content":"That's true, you can use the power to avoid notice after the event. But not during it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:13:59-07:00","id":603187,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input, everybody. So, summarizing what you brought up, I see the following issues:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Size:</b> In RAW, the idea of my player doesn't work because cars should have sizes around 10. For a human-size kindred, 8 is the maximum.</li> <li><b>Attention/Interaction:</b> Driving at high speed through city traffic is calling attention to the car and forcing interaction, so <i>Touch of Shadow</i> will fail.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> However, your reactions are in favour of this idea, and the more I think about it, the more I like it, too. Not how the player proposed it, but the general idea; e.g. tailing someone in an obfuscated car or a obfuscated variant of the stereotypical nondescript surveillance van across the street of your home.<br /> <br /> Let's see what I might offer my player:<br /> <br /> The size issue first. Now that I think of it, I don't like that the maximum size is fixed. I'd like it to depend on the Obfuscate level of the user. An easy way to do this would be to define the &quot;Base Maximum Size&quot; of Obfuscate as (User Size)-1+Obfuscate. So at level 1 it would still be 5 and increase with every level of Obfuscate. A vampire with Obfuscate 5 could use <i>Touch of Shadow</i> on Size 9 objects without penalty and up to Size 12 with penalties. For anything bigger, said vampire would need to use the Oubliette-technique.<br /> Sounds reasonable? Or will that have repercussions for other areas?<br /> If so, one could probably use it as a devotion, like nofather suggested, and make this calculation of maximum size apply to vehicles, only.<br /> <br /> Since 10 is a sports car, one could probably rule that a small vehicle like a motorcycle or a Smart Fortwo might have size 8, a small car like a Ford Fiesta might have 9, mid-sized cars have 10, SUVs and minivans 11, a van 12 and so on.<br /> <br /> The attention/forcing interaction issue, next. With such an application of <i>Touch of Shadow</i>, driving, parking and even tailing should work well, even with an almost derelict vehicle, like Charlaquin suggested. But driving at high speed will draw attention and thus, the Obfuscation will fail. However, as MeetsInTaverns has suggested, it might be used to get rid of pursuers like police afterwards.<br /> <br /> I'd also allow a use of <i>Cloak of Night</i>, since that power is intended to even do outrageous things without drawing attention. However, I'd rule that this is dangerous, because \u2013 even though other traffic participants (&lt;- do you say it like that, in English?) perceive you subconsciously \u2013 their reaction time will be severely hampered. So while audacious Obfuscate users might race invisible cars or motorcycles through the nightly traffic, they'd do so at increased risk of collisions. On top of any situational modifiers for driving at high speed, I'd empose a -3 penalty on the Dexterity + Drive roll and treat any failure as dramatic failure: some spectacular accident. -2 if it's a motorcycle.<br /> <br /> A safer application would be <i>The Familiar Stranger</i>, making the vehicle look like a police car or ambulance.<br /> <br /> My player would probably be happy with that. What do you think? Sounds reasonable?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:39:11-07:00","id":603205,"title":"","content":"Ooh, Familiar Stranger to disguise your car as a police car is a really cool idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T17:31:12-07:00","id":603321,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about the sizes of larger vehicles, I think they're probably larger than that. But as I said, I'm not sure. I neer understood what precisely Size means in volume terms.<br /> <br /> About the new take on the limit, I like it. No sure also if it will have other consequences, but I like it. Or you can just rule it as a 1 XP Devotion with Obfuscate 2 as pre-req, or as part of the effect of a Devotion similar to Cloack the Gathering. Since where talking precisely about the difference between being able or not to cloack a car, I think the Devotion is the best option, it CLEARLY have balance consequences.<br /> <br /> For the penalty, I would make it range from -1 to -5 based on how much the current speed of the vehicle surpasses the average speed of the traffic. That aside, I agree they shouldn't have a normal reaction time.<br /> <br /> Maybe even a -2 extra penalty if the character wants to really pass unoticed: even if the vehicle goes completely unnoticed, the reaction of other cars will be so drastic that the entire thing will attract attention, as a phantom feeling simply made all the drivers to went into temporary madness at the eyes of the witnesses, they included. So a greater penalty could be accepted by the PC to drive in such a way to cause too little a ruckus for the witnesses to notice. Remember, where not talking about normal motion in traffic anymore, but in drivers having to avoid collision with crazy pilot! There are just so much you can do without notice you're doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T00:47:18-07:00","id":603593,"title":"","content":"I'm not good with Size either. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/53237-size\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ess/53237-size</a><br /> It all sounds reasonable enough to me. I think you should have a devotion or merit to cover the Size issue. Otherwise, you would have to get complicated. Your formula would be -1 for Touch of Shadow, -2 for Cloak of Night, and -3 for Familiar Stranger. Technically, you can go to -5 on penalties so you can stretch to cover everything below Oubliette size without gaps as the user gets better at Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> An SUV is Size 15 if that helps. p.182","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 07-26-2015, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T11:07:29-07:00","id":603956,"title":"","content":"The smallest car in the WoD core samples is a compact at Size 9.<br /> <br /> The smallest vehicle is a motorcycle at size 7.<br /> <br /> For the devotion, I'd probably do:<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 2, Vigor 1<br /> +1 maximum size per point of Vigor you possess at the cost of 1 extra Vitae.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty terrible at homebrewing stuff, but Vigor seems to get used a lot with Devotions to beef up the primary Discipline beyond what they can do by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T03:48:34-07:00","id":604576,"title":"","content":"I think it could be a nice Devotion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/824-araknee","name":"Araknee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:44:03-07:00","id":611215,"title":"","content":"The kinds of evasive maneuvers that it would require people to do would be jarring and impossible to keep on an unconscious level, and moreover it's not necessarily true that everyone would even be <i>able </i>to get out of the way in time, much less do so purely instinctively. After all, people can't always get out of the way of cars they <i>can </i>consciously perceive. To use an analogy, being involved in a car chase, even as a &quot;bystander,&quot; is not unlike being attacked.<br /> <br /> Obfuscation works by broadcasting the unconscious message of &quot;nothing to see here, move along.&quot; There's only so much you can impinge on people before that message is rejected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}